reports/2026-08-01-m3-flat-yogunluk/
Logs/

# Track B (vision) training rasters: 780 jpg / 166MB of openly licensed Wikimedia
# + Openverse photos, RE-FETCHABLE by vision/fetch-corpus.sh (md5-dedupes, merges
# manifest). vision/corpus/manifest.json stays tracked, so every photo's source
# URL + licence is preserved and the fetch is reproducible. Nothing in the motor
# line (engine/CMakeLists.txt, engine/tests, scripts/, backend/, web/, contract/)
# reads these files — measured 2026-08-17, zero hits.
vision/corpus/photos/

# stale cmake build trees: engine/.gitignore already covers build/ and build-*/,
# repeated here so a root-level `git status` never surfaces them.
engine/build-*/

# stray root-level ezdxf venv (deleted 2026-08-17): the LIVE one every consumer
# names is engine/.venv-dxf (CMakeLists 403/476, dxf_check.sh, tech_pack_check.sh,
# nest_marker_check.sh, setup-dxf-venv.sh). The root copy had ezdxf only, no
# matplotlib/shapely/PIL, and no file in the tree referenced it.
.venv-dxf/

.rabadon/handoff.md

# rabadon per-agent scratch state, scattered into 9 subdirectories (2026-08-17):
# every agent working in a subdir grows its own .rabadon/, and all of it was
# untracked AND unignored, so every `git status` in this shared tree printed 15
# lines of another agent's noise. That noise is how a staged deletion gets swept
# into someone else's commit. Session transcripts, net/handoff caches and the
# native state dump are per-machine and per-run — never shared history.
# NOT ignored, on purpose: .rabadon/guard.json (the law) and the already-tracked
# .rabadon/state.json files under engine/ and engine/pattern-bridge/.
**/.rabadon/sessions/
**/.rabadon/net.json
**/.rabadon/handoff.md
**/.rabadon/.rabadon/
**/.rabadon/state-native-*.txt
# per-agent counters, same class as the root .rabadon/state.json already ignored
# above. the three state.json files under engine/ and engine/pattern-bridge/ were
# committed before this rule and STAY tracked — gitignore never untracks anything.
**/.rabadon/state.json
core/third_party/.rabadon/

# the drawing path's own venv (numpy/scipy/matplotlib/svgpathtools/pyyaml,
# no GarmentCode): recreated with python3 -m venv + pip install
engine/pattern-bridge/.venv/
